  "scientific_summary": "341690 independent ordinary PASS and cached-literal PASS with an explicit stronger partition: exact one-versus-three TISGM counts for the ferromagnetic hard-core and soft-core Widom-Rowlinson model for all k>=4, Gibbs-measure bridge supplied and valid at theta=0. ROOT SCIENTIFIC EXCLUDE AS ROUTINE, credit 0. Actual basis: arXiv 2401.08706v1 Theorem 3 gives the exact hard-core hinge count, which already forces injectivity and hence strict monotonicity of the theta=0 branch function; the positive-theta case differs only by the elementary positive increasing factor 1/(1-theta/R) and truncation of the interval, and the reviewer supplies the complete all-parameter reduction. Stated limits: this is a routine-adaptation exclusion, not an earlier printed soft-core theorem and not a novelty finding; the upstream hinge proof is abbreviated though its conclusion was independently validated; Rozikov-Khakimov 2015 returned HTTP 404 and is closed and unread; the 2019 final remains closed and unread; source Remark 2 reverses a critical inequality, with no credit for that. Strongest dissent recorded: a deliberate conjecture and an elegant global convexity argument. Formal cost is also high, since the literal needs infinite-tree Gibbs infrastructure. All 96 supplied scopes compared, no family overlap. 153 manifest files, 32 frozen bindings verified. Do not route to formal work.",
